PUBLIC PRIVATE PARTNERSHIP
Features
.The PublicPartner in ther PPP: The public partner in the PPP model are government entities
i.e. ministeries, government department, municipalities or state owned enterprise. The
private partners can be local or foreign investors with technical or financial expertise related
to the project.
2 The Role of Public Sector in PPP: The role of public sector in PPP is to ensure social
obligations are fulfilled and sector reforms and public investment are successfully met.
.The Role of Private Sector: The role of private sector is to make use of its expertise in
operation, managing tasks and innovation to run the business efficiently.
Contract between Public Sector and Private Party: PPP is a contract between public sector
authority and private party, in which the private party provides a public service and bears
financial, technical and operational risk.
